#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:7
msgid "Testing with pre-release binaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:9
msgid ""
"Many ROS packages are provided as pre-built binaries. Usually, you will get "
"the released version of binaries when following :doc:`../../Get-Started/"
"Installation`. There are also pre-released versions of binaries that are "
"useful for testing before making an official release. This article describes "
"several options if you would like to try out pre-released versions of ROS "
"binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:14
msgid ""
"When packages are released into a ROS distribution (using bloom), the "
"buildfarm builds them into deb packages which are stored temporarily in the "
"**building** apt repository. As dependent packages are rebuilt, an automatic "
"process periodically synchronizes the packages in **building** to a "
"secondary repository called **ros-testing**. **ros-testing** is intended as "
"a soaking area where developers and bleeding-edge users may give the "
"packages extra testing, before they are manually synced into the public ros "
"repository from which users typically install packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:18
msgid ""
"Approximately every two weeks, the rosdistro's release manager manually "
"synchronizes the contents of **ros-testing** into the **main** ROS "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:21
msgid "deb testing repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:23
msgid ""
"For Debian-based operating systems, you can install binary packages from the "
"**ros-testing** repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:25
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a working ROS 2 installation from deb packages (see :doc:"
"`../../Get-Started/Installation`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:27
msgid ""
"Install the ros2-testing-apt-source package. This will automatically "
"uninstall the ros2-apt-source package since only one repository may be "
"enabled at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:30
msgid "$ sudo apt install -y ros2-testing-apt-source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:34
msgid "Update the apt index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:36
msgid "$ sudo apt update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:40
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:86
msgid ""
"You can now install individual packages from the testing repository, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:42
msgid "$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-my-just-released-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:46
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can move your entire ROS 2 installation to the testing "
"repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:48
msgid "$ sudo apt dist-upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:52
msgid ""
"Once you are finished testing, you can switch back to the normal repository "
"by re-installing the ros-apt-source package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:54
msgid "$ sudo apt install -y ros2-apt-source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:58
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:99
msgid "and doing an update and upgrade:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:60
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt dist-upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:67
msgid "RHEL testing repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:69
msgid ""
"For RHEL you can install binary packages from the **ros-testing** "
"repository, by enabling the testing repository on the source configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:71
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a working ROS 2 installation for rpm packages (see the :"
"doc:`RHEL installation instructions <../../Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-"
"Install-RPMs>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:73
msgid "Enable testing and disable main repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:75
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf config-manager --set-enabled ros2-testing\n"
"$ sudo dnf config-manager --set-disabled ros2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:80
msgid "Update the dnf index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:82
msgid "$ sudo dnf update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:88
msgid "$ sudo dnf install ros-rolling-my-just-released-package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:92
msgid ""
"Once you are finished testing, you can switch back to the normal repository "
"by re-enabling the main repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:94
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf config-manager --set-disabled ros2-testing\n"
"$ sudo dnf config-manager --set-enabled ros2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:101
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf update\n"
"$ sudo dnf system-upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:109
msgid "Binary archives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:111
msgid ""
"For core packages, we run nightly packaging jobs for Ubuntu Linux, RHEL, and "
"Windows. These packaging jobs produce archives with pre-built binaries that "
"can be downloaded and extracted to your filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:114
msgid ""
"Make sure you have all dependencies installed according to the :doc:`latest "
"development setup <../../Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Latest-"
"Development-Setup>` for your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:116
msgid ""
"Go to https://ci.ros2.org/view/packaging/ and select a packaging job from "
"the list corresponding to your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:118
msgid ""
"Under the heading \"Last Successful Artifacts\" you should see a download "
"link (e.g. for Windows, ``ros2-package-windows-AMD64.zip``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:120
msgid "Download and extract the archive to your file system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:122
msgid ""
"To use the binary archive installation, source the ``setup.*`` file that can "
"be found in the root of the archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:126
msgid "Ubuntu Linux and RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:128
msgid "$ source path/to/extracted/archive/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:132
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:134
msgid "$ call path\\to\\extracted\\archive\\setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:139
msgid "Docker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:141
msgid ""
"For Ubuntu Linux, there is also a nightly Docker image based on the nightly "
"binary archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:143
msgid "Pull the Docker image:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:145
msgid "$ docker pull osrf/ros2:nightly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:149
msgid "Start an interactive container:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:151
msgid "$ docker run -it osrf/ros2:nightly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Testing/Testing.rst:155
msgid ""
"For support on running GUI applications in Docker, take a look at the "
"tutorial `User GUI's with Docker <https://wiki.ros.org/docker/Tutorials/"
"GUI>`_ or the tool `rocker <https://github.com/osrf/rocker>`_."
msgstr ""
